  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acting Now for Food Security and Resilient Food Systems - Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme is implemented to respond to the current food crisis in Kenya. The programme supports smallholders to increase the production and quality of fruits and vegetables, cereals, pulses and goat herding and so increase their incomes, reduce production costs and improve market access. This is done by supporting smallholders on timely planting, field management, harvesting and post harvest management technologies directly, via lead partners and by capacitated agricultural extension officers. We contribute to better service delivery by working with service providers improving their farm and storage services and offering alternative local low cost farm inputs. The Gender Action Learning System (GALS) methodology is used to engage men and boys in the promotion of women&#x2019;s economic empowerment and addressing unequal gender norms and roles.</narrative>
  </description>
